{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"profile":1,"footerKeywords":13,"hero":111,"footer":124},{"name":2,"surname":3,"jobPosition":4,"presentationHtml":5,"email":6,"github":7,"linkedin":10},"Alessandro","Quets","Digital Designer & Frontend Developer","\u003Cp>My background is in communication and information design. Over the past three years, I’ve worked with startups in DeFi and crypto, designing interfaces and building the frontend behind them.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>My work has ranged from trading products and design systems to a blockchain rebrand. Across these projects, I’ve been interested in the same challenge: helping people understand and use complex products.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Alongside product work, I’m a teaching assistant in interaction design at Politecnico di Milano.\u003C/p>","alessandroquets@gmail.com",{"label":8,"url":9},"MingoBerlingo","https://github.com/MingoBerlingo",{"label":11,"url":12},"linkedin.com/in/alessandro-quets-07531a3b6","https://www.linkedin.com/in/alessandro-quets-07531a3b6/",[14,19,23,27,31,35,39,43,47,51,55,59,63,67,71,75,79,83,87,91,95,99,103,107],{"id":15,"label":16,"order":17,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c578","UX / UI",0,true,{"id":20,"label":21,"order":22,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c57c","Web Design",1,{"id":24,"label":25,"order":26,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c580","Creative Coding",2,{"id":28,"label":29,"order":30,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c584","Dataviz",3,{"id":32,"label":33,"order":34,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c588","Interaction",4,{"id":36,"label":37,"order":38,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c58c","Svelte",5,{"id":40,"label":41,"order":42,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c590","React",6,{"id":44,"label":45,"order":46,"showInFooter":18},"6ae4b0409463a3b51b42c594","Branding",7,{"id":48,"label":49,"order":50,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb827","Design Systems",8,{"id":52,"label":53,"order":54,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb82b","Prototyping",9,{"id":56,"label":57,"order":58,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb82f","Frontend",10,{"id":60,"label":61,"order":62,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb833","Accessibility",11,{"id":64,"label":65,"order":66,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb837","TypeScript",12,{"id":68,"label":69,"order":70,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb83b","Component Libraries",13,{"id":72,"label":73,"order":74,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb83f","Motion Design",14,{"id":76,"label":77,"order":78,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8615526b10afc982fb843","Data Storytelling",15,{"id":80,"label":81,"order":82,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea691","Figma",16,{"id":84,"label":85,"order":86,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea699","Information Design",17,{"id":88,"label":89,"order":90,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea69d","Interaction Design",18,{"id":92,"label":93,"order":94,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a1","UI Engineering",19,{"id":96,"label":97,"order":98,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a5","Design Tokens",20,{"id":100,"label":101,"order":102,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6a9","AI Workflows",21,{"id":104,"label":105,"order":106,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6ad","DeFi",22,{"id":108,"label":109,"order":110,"showInFooter":18},"6ae8fdd6321ceae5155ea6b1","Web3",23,{"greeting":112,"nameLine":113,"introduction":114,"homepageIntroduction":115,"featuredProjects":116,"homepageImages":123},"Hey!","I’m Alessandro Quets.","I’m a Digital Designer & Frontend Developer based in Lecco, Italy 🇮🇹","I care about how an interface looks [eye], how it feels, and how it works.\n\nI shape interactions, build design systems, and carry those decisions into production [components] Working in both Figma [figma] and code [code] lets me keep refining the details as I build.\n\nI can sit in a design review and open a pull request [pull-request] on the same day.",[117,119,121],{"id":118},"6ac8b04e1617bfc2eb4349f3",{"id":120},"6ae9da5d2756dce0f10604ee",{"id":122},"6aad520fe6ebe5c3c1970865",[],{"heading":125,"keywordsHeading":126,"signature":127},"Make it clear.\nMake it feel right.","A few things I work with","In ♥ with pixels"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"suggestedProjects":1,"project":28},[2,17],{"id":3,"slug":4,"title":5,"shortTitle":6,"tagline":7,"year":8,"isFeatured":9,"featuredImage":10,"videoCover":16},"6ae9da5d2756dce0f10604ee","aura","Aura.money","Aura","Building a social trading app","2025-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",true,{"previewDataURL":11,"url":12,"alt":13,"width":14,"height":15},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/aura-cover.png","Aura trading app on a phone against a blue sky and clouds",1920,1080,null,{"id":18,"slug":19,"title":20,"shortTitle":21,"tagline":22,"year":23,"isFeatured":9,"featuredImage":24,"videoCover":16},"6aad520fe6ebe5c3c1970865","smilee","Smilee Finance","Smilee","Building a scalable DeFi ecosystem","2025-05-01T12:00:00.000Z",{"previewDataURL":25,"url":26,"alt":27,"width":14,"height":15},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/smilee-cover.png","Smilee Finance cover",{"id":29,"slug":30,"title":31,"shortTitle":31,"tagline":32,"year":33,"isFeatured":9,"isMinor":34,"client":31,"role":35,"output":36,"featuredImage":37,"videoCover":16,"links":41,"collaborators":45,"contentHtml":46,"createdAt":47,"updatedAt":48},"6ac8b04e1617bfc2eb4349f3","berachain","Berachain","Designing the face of a blockchain","2026-04-01T12:00:00.000Z",false,"Design & Frontend Lead","Web Apps",{"previewDataURL":38,"url":39,"alt":40,"width":14,"height":15},"data:image/jpeg;base64,","/media/berachain-cover.png","Berachain landing page hero section",[42],{"label":43,"url":44},"berachain.com","https://www.berachain.com/",[],"\u003Ch1>Overview\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Berachain\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Berachain is a high-performance EVM-compatible Blockchain built on Proof-of-Liquidity. It features apps for swapping tokens, earning rewards, minting its stablecoin and lending. I joined the team at a pivot point and helped transition to better address a new institutional and business oriented target.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-bento.png\" alt=\"Berachain bento presentation\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>The challenge\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>From Degen to Business\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Berachain had always spoken the language of crypto natives: irreverent, full of inside jokes, and made for a community that already knew the game. But the audience was changing. I redesigned the landing page to speak to businesses and institutions too, keeping the bear’s personality but trading the degen tone for clarity, credibility, and a more structured story.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The same shift ran through the rest of the brand. I refined the icons of the ecosystem apps, and I led the rebrand of Honey into BUSD, Berachain’s native stablecoin, reworking both its name and its visual identity to fit a more institutional audience.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-landing-before-after-comparison.png\" alt=\"Berachain landing page before and after the redesign\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-2\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-x-posts.png\" alt=\"Berachain X posts using the new branding\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-busd.png\" alt=\"HONEY token rebranded to BUSD\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cdiv data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cvideo data-deferred preload=\"none\" poster=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" data-src=\"/media/berachain-landing-scroll.webm\" data-autoplay muted loop playsinline>\u003C/video>\u003Cnoscript>\u003Cvideo controls preload=\"none\" poster=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" src=\"/media/berachain-landing-scroll.webm\" muted loop playsinline>\u003C/video>\u003C/noscript>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>UX improvements\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Reshaping the swap experience\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>BeraHub is the biggest app in the ecosystem, with 15k users and $2B in TVL, and swapping is where most people start. I reworked the swap experience adding the UX for two new features: \u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Cross-chain bridge\u003C/strong>, enabling users to move assets between Berachain and other blockchains.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Fiat onramp\u003C/strong> powered by Alchemy Pay, making it possible to buy crypto with card or bank transfer.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Getting into the ecosystem now takes a few clicks instead of a few tutorials.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-1\">\u003Cdiv data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cvideo data-deferred preload=\"none\" poster=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" data-src=\"/media/berachain-crosschain-bridge.webm\" data-autoplay muted loop playsinline>\u003C/video>\u003Cnoscript>\u003Cvideo controls preload=\"none\" poster=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" src=\"/media/berachain-crosschain-bridge.webm\" muted loop playsinline>\u003C/video>\u003C/noscript>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>Design System\u003C/h1>\u003Ch2>Tidying up the foundations\u003C/h2>\u003Cp>Behind the apps, I reworked Berachain’s design system to be more consistent, scalable, and easier to maintain. I work on it both in Figma and directly in the codebase, so that what’s designed is what actually ships.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>On top of that, I keep improving the ecosystem’s core apps, BeraHub, Bend, and BUSD, working on features, architecture, and interface so they feel like parts of the same product.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout media-layout--grid\">\u003Cdiv class=\"media-layout-row media-layout-row--columns-2\">\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-ui-atoms.png\" alt=\"Bera Design System UI atoms\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1600\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-media data-media-state=\"loading\" class=\"media-frame\">\u003Cimg data-preview src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"media-preview\" />\u003Cimg src=\"/media/berachain-ui-molecules.png\" alt=\"Bera Design System UI molecules\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1600\" loading=\"lazy\" />\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>\u003Ch1>What i learned\u003C/h1>\u003Cp>Working on Berachain taught me that good design in Web3 is less about novelty and more about trust. Changing a brand’s tone is a design decision, a design system only matters when it makes it to production, and the best onboarding flow is the one that makes a complex process feel simple.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr />\u003C/p>","2026-10-09T09:13:50.291Z","2026-10-30T14:19:43.923Z"],"uses":{"params":["slug"],"parent":1}}]}
